PATCH: zephyr_ipv6_nbr_ns_pending_leak — free abandoned NS solicitation
=======================================================================

Written against: Zephyr 4.4.x  (verified present in v4.4.1 and main, 2026-06)
Target platform: ESP32-S3 on Zephyr RTOS, IPv6
Application:     /workspace/projects/hello_eink  (LLSS e-ink client)

SUMMARY
-------
net_ipv6_send_ns() allocates a Neighbor Solicitation net_pkt up front. When the
target neighbor already has a solicitation pending, the function appends the
caller's data packet to the pending queue and returns early ("Let the system
timeout and then send the NS again") WITHOUT freeing the NS packet it just
built. The only success-path unref is in net_send_data() -> L2 send, which is
past the early return and never reached. Every packet sent to an INCOMPLETE
neighbor that already has a pending solicitation leaks one TX net_pkt.

ROOT CAUSE / FIX
----------------
Add net_pkt_unref(pkt) before the already-pending early return. We deliberately
do not send this NS, so the built packet must be released.

Found on hardware (TX-pool drain over hours of server-reconnect churn); zero NS
leaked after the fix. Full writeup: NETBUF_LEAK_ADVENTURE.md.

--- 8< --- diff --- 8< ---
--- a/subsys/net/ip/ipv6_nbr.c	2026-06-19 17:30:04.518002489 +0000
+++ b/subsys/net/ip/ipv6_nbr.c	2026-06-19 17:30:04.518130699 +0000
@@ -2176,7 +2176,13 @@
 					pending, nbr);
 			}
 
-			/* Let the system timeout and then send the NS again */
+			/* Let the system timeout and then send the NS again.
+			 * A packet is already pending for this neighbor, so we do
+			 * NOT send this NS; release the solicitation packet built
+			 * above or it leaks -- net_send_data() below (which hands
+			 * pkt to the TX path that unrefs it) is never reached.
+			 */
+			net_pkt_unref(pkt);
 			net_ipv6_nbr_unlock();
 			return 0;
 		}
